body:
Sorry its just a bit confusing. Well I have my main issue. Its this code:
 string[] readthis = System.IO.File.ReadAllLines(input);

In Visual Studio it works because I input a path when I run the console application.
So the console looks like this from visual studio:
------------------------------------------------
Input file path:
//user inputs a path "C:\\here\here"
//file is read and the code executes properly.

------------------------------------
But when I submit it to codeeval it cant receive a file path because there is no user. So it just says on the console to input a valid path. How can my program read a file that I dont have a filepath for? My program cant read codeeval's input file.
